<% content_for :page_title, "DecisionDesk — Eligibility Screening Platform" %>

<section class="hero container">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow">Configurable intake & decisioning</div>
    <h1>Professional eligibility screening for complex, evolving workflows.</h1>
    <p class="lead">DecisionDesk is a business-facing intake platform for guided screening and recommendation workflows. It guides applicants through a branching questionnaire, produces a clear outcome, and gives administrators a searchable dashboard of submissions and decision paths.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="/app" class="button">Launch Live Demo</a>
      <a href="#architecture" class="button button-ghost">See Architecture</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-microcopy">Built on Rails with JSON endpoints, persistent sample data, and one-click reset controls for repeatable walkthroughs.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-visual card">
    <div class="window-head">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="mock-screen">
      <div class="mock-sidebar">
        <div class="mock-pill active"></div>
        <div class="mock-pill"></div>
        <div class="mock-pill"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-main">
        <div class="mock-stat-row">
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-table"></div>
        <div class="mock-flow">
          <div class="mock-node active"></div>
          <div class="mock-node"></div>
          <div class="mock-node"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="features" class="container section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="eyebrow">What it demonstrates</div>
    <h2>Core features for complex screening workflows.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid three-up">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Branching intake</h3>
      <p>Applicants move through a conditional, multi-step questionnaire that adapts to prior answers and finishes with a clear recommendation.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Admin review</h3>
      <p>Administrators can search, filter, and inspect submissions, including a readable view of the exact decision path taken.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Resettable demo data</h3>
      <p>Sample data can be restored with one click, making the application easy to demonstrate repeatedly without manual cleanup.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section split-section">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Suggested use cases</div>
    <h2>Broad enough to travel across industries.</h2>
    <p class="muted">The same intake-and-decision pattern can support benefits screening, operations triage, service routing, onboarding workflows, or internal review pipelines. That makes DecisionDesk adaptable across a wide range of operational contexts.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card bullet-card">
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Eligibility and benefits screening</li>
      <li>Customer or partner intake</li>
      <li>Operations triage and routing</li>
      <li>Compliance or review workflows</li>
      <li>Admin dashboards and searchable submissions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="architecture" class="container section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="eyebrow">Architecture</div>
    <h2>Built for maintainable application workflows.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid two-up">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Workflow-driven application design</h3>
      <p>DecisionDesk combines Rails controllers, ERB views, JSON endpoints, and reusable service objects to keep screening logic, intake flow, and administrator review aligned in one application.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Operational simplicity where it helps</h3>
      <p>A SQL database backs the primary application flow so submissions, recommendations, and administrator review can all run on a more production-shaped persistence layer.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="cta card">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Live demo</div>
      <h2>Try the screening flow and inspect the admin dashboard.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Use the sample data, submit a new screening, and reset everything back to its initial state when you are done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a href="/app" class="button">Open Demo App</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
